rrent card, highlighted chart point, sheet presentation)\" — only these four named. I'll keep button enabled blue.\n- Card preview: shows the number typed so far → \"5412 7534 0089 2216\" formatted in groups.\n\n**05_Payment:**\n- Background light\n- Header: \"Payment\" centered title (+ maybe back? brief says Actions: Cancel · Pay now only. So header just title, no back icon; Cancel is the dismiss.)\n- Payee: \"PAYING\" eyebrow + Avatar_Robert_Dawson (72×72 circle) + \"Robert Dawson\"\n- Amount: $50.00 large (48 Bold)\n- Note field: \"Add a note\" — empty input with placeholder \"Add a note\". Brief: Note: \"Add a note\" (empty). So a text field with placeholder \"Add a note\". \n- Card selector: Maria's Visa card (mini card or row): use Card_Texture_Coral mini card with number \"4225 9765 0008 6141\" or a row: card art thumbnail + \"Maria's Visa card\" + \"card 1 of 3\"? Brief: Card: Maria's Visa card (as on 03_Wallet) · card 1 of 3. I'll do a horizontal row: mini card art (60×38) + \"Maria's Visa\" + \"•••• 6141\" + chevron + \"1 of 3\" badge. Or show the full card. Space: 812 height. Let me lay out: status bar 44, header ~56, payee section ~140, amount ~120, note field ~73, card row ~76, Pay now button 56, home indicator. Fits.\n- Buttons: \"Cancel\" (secondary/gray or text button) and \"Pay now\" (primary blue). Two buttons bottom: Cancel could be a text button centered, Pay now full width. I'll do: Pay now full-width primary; Cancel as gray tonal button above it or side-by-side. Side-by-side: Cancel 100 wide + Pay now flexible. I'll do stacked: Pay now primary full width, Cancel text button below? Better: two side-by-side buttons: Cancel (light gray fill #EEEDF2, text #1A1A1F) and Pay now (blue). Hmm, given \"Cancel\" usually dismisses: I'll do Cancel as a full-width quiet text button under Pay now.\n\n**06_Receipt:**\n- White/light background\n- Header: \"Receipt\" centered, Icon_Share right\n- Receipt card (white, radius 16, shadow): centered \"CASH RECEIPT\" (letterspaced), date \"20.08.2020\", divider, rows: Amount $40.00, Service Fee $2.82, Internet Charge $7.18, divider, Total $50.00 (bold), barcode Barcode_Receipt centered, maybe \"Thank you\" not needed. Keep exact copy.\n- \"Home\" button bottom → 02_Home.\n\n**Components to build in workspace (as COMPONENT nodes):**\n- Button (clone from reference: instance? I can create instances of the reference components directly into workspace — but reference is read-only. Copying instances into workspace page is allowed: \"New frames, reusable components and prototype connections are allowed in this workspace\". The brief says \"Use the logo, illustrations... from 04 · Media\" and \"reuse the components in 02 · Components\". I'll create my own components in workspace that wrap/instance the reference media components. \n\nWait — can I create instances of components from another page in the same file? Yes! Instances can live anywhere in the same document. `figma.createComponentFromNode(component)` or `comp.createInstance()` and append to my frames. The media components (Logo_Expenio etc.) are COMPONENT nodes (symbol type in metadata = component). So I can do `figma.getNodeById(\"6:10\").createInstance()` and add to my design. That's the cleanest \"reuse\" — actual component instances.\n\nPlan for component architecture in workspace:\n- **Icon buttons**: IconButton (44×44 circle, white fill) with icon instance inside.\n- **Header**: NavigationBar component (title + left/right slots) — but slots vary per screen. To keep it manageable, I'll create a few header variants as components: Header_Wallet (back+title+add), Header_Title (title only), Header_Receipt (title+share). Or just build headers inline per screen but as components with text override. Component reuse is evaluated — I should create real components:\n  - `Icon / IconButton` component\n  - `Button / Primary` (instance of given Button? The given Button component 1:23 is fixed text \"Get Started\". I can instance it an