eld instance in the screen frame) — visually equivalent, simpler. Actually overlaying icons on top of instances in the parent frame is easy and robust. I'll do that for MC logo and help icon.\n  - `Transaction Row` component: 44 icon tile + title + date + amount.\n  - `Transaction List` maybe not; place 3 instances in a white card container.\n  - `Section Header` component: title + optional action (\"See all\").\n  - `Payment Card` component (Maria's Visa, full size) — used on 03_Wallet (with \"current card\" state = highlighted border? \"current card in the wallet\" state — the pagination dot 1 active covers \"card 1 of 3\"; also maybe the card has a selected ring. I'll show dots + card labeled). Also used smaller on 05_Payment? Payment uses \"card 1 of 3\" too — I'll instance the full card scaled? Scale would distort text. Instead make PaymentCard row: mini card thumb + text. I'll build `Card / Mini` separate or just a row built inline. Let me make `Card Row / Visa` component used in 05.\n  - `Promo Card` component.\n  - `Balance Card` component (home hero card).\n  - `Expenses Chart` component (vector curve + points + labels).\n  - `Status Bar` & `Home Indicator`: instance the given components directly.\n  - `Sheet` maybe not a component.\n  - `Receipt Card` component? Used once; fine to build inline but components earn reuse points. I'll componentize: TransactionRow, SectionHeader, IconButton, ButtonPrimary, ButtonSecondary, BalanceCard, ChartCard, PromoCard, PaymentCard(Visa), ReceiptCard? Receipt used once. Enough.\n\n**Prototype wiring:**\n- 01_Get_Started: Button → 02_Home (on click, navigation)\n- 02_Home: balance card (whole card or chevron) → 03_Wallet; \"See all\" → 03_Wallet; FAB (+) → 05_Payment\n- 03_Wallet: back icon → 02_Home; add-card icon → 04_Add_Card (open as... presentation: \"sheet over 03_Wallet\" — since 04 is its own frame containing the sheet visual, link is just Navigation to 04_Add_Card; I'll set animation to \"Open\" with default)\n- 04_Add_Card: \"Add new card\" button → 03_Wallet; close icon → 03_Wallet\n- 05_Payment: Pay now → 06_Receipt; Cancel → 02_Home\n- 06_Receipt: Home button → 02_Home\n\n**Implementation approach with use_figma:**\nMultiple calls, each ≤50k chars:\n1. Setup: load fonts; create page-local \"Design System\" section? Build components on workspace page in a components area (x offset -600 or above frames). Order:\n   a. Create text styles + color styles (helps consistency) — optional but good. figma.createTextStyle(), createPaintStyle().\n   b. Build base components: IconButton(+variants via separate comps), SectionHeader, TransactionRow, Buttons, TextField base, ChartCard, BalanceCard, PromoCard, PaymentCard, MiniCard.\n2. Build 01_Get_Started.\n3. Build 02_Home.\n4. Build 03_Wallet.\n5. Build 04_Add_Card.\n6. Build 05_Payment.\n7. Build 06_Receipt.\n8. Prototype wiring.\n9. Screenshots + fixes.\n\nImportant plugin API gotchas:\n- Load fonts before creating text: `await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Inter\", style:\"Regular\"/\"Medium\"/\"Semi Bold\"/\"Bold\"})`. Also monospace: try \"Roboto Mono\" styles \"Medium\"/\"Regular\" — wrap in try/catch.\n- setCurrentPageAsync to switch to workspace page: `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(figma.getNodeById(\"8:2\"))` — actually setCurrentPageAsync takes a PageNode.\n- Creating instances of components from other pages is fine.\n- For text on instances: instance.children — the given Button has text child directly.\n- Vector chart: create VectorNode via figma.createVector() with vectorPaths = [{windingRule:'NONZERO', data:'M ...'}] — vectorPaths setter works with path data using only M/L/C/Q/Z... Actually vectorPaths data supports M, L, C, Q, Z commands? Figma vectorPaths supports a subset: M, L, Q, C, Z. Yes.\n- Gradients: GradientPaint with gradientTransform + gradientStops. gradientTransform is [[a,b,tx],[c,d,ty]] mapping unit space.\n- Images: Card_Texture_Coral is a component (5:10) — instance it and resize; it presumably contains an image fill. Avatars contain image fills. Just instance them.\n- The status bar glyphs are black; on light bg fine. On 04 sheet dim area, still fine (black glyphs on dimmed white). On coral card no status bar overlap.\n- Cropping avatars to circle: the avatar components are square-ish images (Maria 108×72? that's odd - maybe includes padding. Avatar_Maria_Lopez symbol is 108×72 — the photo may be within. Let me inspect avatar internals before using. Also avatar in header should be circular ~44. I can instance the avatar component and apply cornerRadius on the instance (cornerRadius on instance root applies rounded rect mask? cornerRadius on a frame instance rounds children if clipsContent). If the component root is a frame with image fill, setting cornerRadius=22 + clipsContent works. Need to inspect. Similarly Robert 72×72.\n\nLet me inspect the media component internals (5:2, 5:4, 5:10, 5:6, 5:8, 5:3, 6:11, 6:2, merchants, icons) — check root types and fills so I can size/round them properly.","signature":"40b5e2835e7942e78c18de63"}],"id":"b518fc98-db92-406a-bc49-ae69461c3b94","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259a9f97-bab6-42ed-a1f7-e48e66488de3","uuid":"691e2cf7-d656-4ed2-974c-e3ea78734eda","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:29:23.445Z","thinking_duration_ms":95744}
