onents? Overkill. Alternative: IconButton component with NO icon child; place icon instance absolutely on top in screen frame. Then \"component\" is just the circle. Simpler: build icon buttons inline per screen (circle + icon), and componentize bigger things. But state design & reuse evaluated... The brief item 4: \"Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\" Headers as components! Headers differ per screen (left/right content). Make Header component with slots as empty frames? Slot pattern: component contains left slot frame (40×40), title text, right slot frame (40×40); instances: for screens without buttons, hide left/right slots (visibility override) and set title. For Wallet: need back icon + add icon INSIDE instance slots — can't insert into instance children!\n\nInstance limitations: cannot add children to instances. So slot must pre-exist in component containing... I can put the icon instances in the component's slots and toggle visibility per usage. Different icons per screen → need all icon variants present, toggle visibility. That's hacky but works: slots contain both Icon_Back and Icon_Add_Card (both hidden by default), show needed. Header variants via visibility overrides. OK — Header/Bar component: 375×56: leftBtn 40×40 circle white (contains Icon_Back hidden + Icon_Add_Card hidden? two icons stacked), title centered 18 SemiBold, rightBtn 40×40 circle (contains Icon_Close hidden, Icon_Share hidden, Icon_Plus hidden). Screens:\n- 02 Home: no header bar (custom greeting) — separate.\n- 03 Wallet: left=Back visible, title=\"Wallet\", right=Add_Card visible.\n- 04 sheet: left=hidden, title=\"Add new card\", right=Close visible. (in sheet, white bg)\n- 05 Payment: title=\"Payment\", both hidden.\n- 06 Receipt: title=\"Receipt\", right=Share visible.\nWorks with visibility + text override.\n\n3. SectionHeader component: 343×24: title 18 SemiBold + action \"See all\" 14 Medium brand