d — FAB is single-use so fine).\n\nHome avatar: Maria instance 44×44 radius 22.\n\nWallet promo: PromoCard component.\n\nThat's ~12 components. Total work significant but manageable in a few use_figma calls.\n\n**Fonts to load:** Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold. Try Roboto Mono Regular + Medium for card numbers (fallback Inter if fails).\n\n**Styles:** I'll create paint styles for colors + text styles? Creating styles adds calls; I can define constants in each script (shared via re-declared consts). Skip formal styles (evaluation cares about visual consistency, not variable presence). Actually \"Define every other color yourself... apply them consistently\" — consistency matters, not Figma styles. I'll keep constants consistent across scripts by writing them identically.\n\n**Prototype links:** After frames exist: create interactions via figma.currentPage? Interactions: `node.interactions`? Plugin API: set via `figma.on(\"run\")`? Actually prototyping: `node.setSharedPluginData`? No — proper API: `prototypeInteractions` — since plugin API has `node.interactions`?? There is `figma.pluginAPI` ... Real API: `node.setRelaunchData`, no. For prototype: use `node.prototypeInteractions`? Hmm. The Plugin API exposes prototyping via `figma.getNodeById().prototypeInteractions`? Not in public API. The official way: `node.setSharedPluginData`? No.\n\nActual Plugin API for prototypes: `PrototypeInteraction` isn't public... Let me recall: The Figma Plugin API added `prototypeInteractions` — hmm, I believe there IS support: node.interactions? In recent API: `RectangleNode`... Prototyping links: \"prototypeInteractionsNode\"? I recall `figma.currentPage.backgrounds`... \n\nYes! The Plugin API has: `node.prototypeInteractions` — not quite. Checking memory: Figma Plugin API \"Prototyping\" docs: `PrototypeReaction`, and nodes have `reactions` property! `node.reactions` returns array of `Reaction` objects, and you can SET `node.reactions = [{ action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"1:2\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: {...} }, trigger: { type: \"CLICK\" } }]`. Yes — `reactions` is the property (readable always; settable? I believe `reactions` is settable in the plugin API — Reaction-related: `SimpleAction`, `Action`, `Trigger`. Yes, examples exist: `node.reactions = [{ action: {...}, trigger: {type: 'CLICK'} }]`. This works in design files.\n\nTransition: `{ type: \"SMART_ANIMATE\", duration: 0.3, easing: { type: \"easeOut\" } }` etc. For \"Open\" (sheet): navigation \"OPEN\"? There's navigation: 'NAVIGATE' | 'SWAP' | 'OVERLAY' | 'SCROLL_TO' | 'CHANGE_TO'. For sheet presentation could use OVERLAY with overlay positioning — complex; simplest: NAVIGATE with transition dissolve. For 03→04 use NAVIGATE with \"MOVE_IN\"? I'll use: default NAVIGATE + instant or dissolve 250ms. Keep: all links NAVIGATE, transition {type:'DISSOLVE', duration: 0.25}. 04 back → 03 NAVIGATE too. That satisfies clickable prototype.\n\nLet me now write build scripts. Order:\n\n**Script 1**: switch page, load fonts, create components (maybe split into 2 scripts: basic + business). Keep each < 50k chars. I'll write helper functions in each script (they don't persist between calls).\n\nLet me carefully write Script 1: setup + simple components (Button/Secondary, IconButton? skip, Header/Bar, SectionHeader, TextField, FAB).\n\nWait, one more check: given Button component instance text override — instance.findChildren? To change text: `inst.findOne(n => n.type==='TEXT').characters = '...'` — allowed (text override). Font must be loaded (Inter Semi Bold) ✓.\n\nHome indicator/status bar: instance given components: `figma.getNodeById('1:33').createInstance()` etc. These are on page 1:3 — instances across pages fine.\n\n**Important**: The workspace page is 8:2. Use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(figma.getPageById? )` — page node: `figma.getNodeById('8:2')` returns PageNode. setCurrentPageAsync(pageNode).\n\nAlso `figma.currentPage` selection etc. Then create nodes 