e on 04 to white. Dim over light gray gives mid-gray; black OK contrast ~4:1. Keep black (simpler, consistent) — or lighten dim to 0.38. Fine.\n\nAlso 04 frame: which wallet elements visible: status bar, header (Wallet), card top portion, promo? Sheet covers from y=222. Card 112..311 → top 110px visible under dim. Good context.\n\nFrame backgrounds: set frame.fill = bg color. 01 white.\n\nAlso add small page labels? No — frame names carry. I'll add a caption text above each frame (name + purpose) — helpful but optional; skip to keep canvas clean? Add tiny gray labels — they help evaluation readability. I'll add.\n\nLet me also confirm: \"The brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit\" — fine.\n\nWrite Script 1 now: page switch, fonts, constants, helpers, components: Secondary button, Header bar, SectionHeader, TextField, TransactionRow. Return IDs.\n\nScript 2: business components: BalanceCard, PaymentCard, MiniCardRow, PromoCard, ChartCard, ReceiptCard, FAB.\n\nScript 3: frames 01 + 02.\nScript 4: frames 03 + 04.\nScript 5: frames 05 + 06.\nScript 6: prototype wiring.\nScript 7: screenshot checks + fixes.\n\nFont loading: Inter Regular/Medium/Semi Bold/Bold + Roboto Mono Medium (try). \n\nHelpers in each script (redeclare): solid(hex), S(hex,o), text(opts), mk(...). Keep scripts compact.\n\nLet me write Script 1.\n\nNote about creating component inside a container: components can live nested in frames — I'll place them loose on page at components area (x= -500? or y=1100). Put at y=1100 row.\n\nAlso: `figma.getNodeById` deprecated in favor of `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync` — older sync version still works in most environments. The MCP environment probably supports both; sync version may be deprecated but functional. I'll use sync with try/catch fallback? Use `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` (await) — it exists in current API. I'll use await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(...).\n\nText creation: `const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'}; t.characters='...'; t.fontSize=...` — need font loaded before setting fontName. Load all first.\n\nlineHeight: {unit:'PIXELS', value:24} for multi-line.\n\nletterSpacing: {unit:'PERCENT', value:8}.\n\nText align center with fixed width: t.resize(w,h); t.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER'; textAutoResize default 'WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT' — after resize it becomes 'NONE'? Setting resize sets box; then set textAutoResize='NONE' explicitly then resize. I'll set t.textAutoResize='NONE'; t.resize(w,h); t.textAlignHorizontal='CENTER'.\n\nRight-aligned amounts: easier: set textAutoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT then position x = right - t.width (after characters set, width available).\n\nFor text inside auto-layout, alignment via layout.\n\nOK, writing Script 1:\n\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst fonts = [['Inter','Regular'],['Inter','Medium'],['Inter','Semi Bold'],['Inter','Bold'],['Roboto Mono','Medium']];\nfor (const [f,s] of fonts){ try{ await figma.loadFontAsync({family:f,style:s}); }catch(e){ console.log('missing',f,s); } }\nconst H=(x)=>x; // noop\nfunction hex(h,o=1){const n=parseInt(h,16);return {r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255};}\nfunction solid(h,o=1){return {type:'SOLID',color:hex(h),opacity:o};}\nfunction T(name,chars,fam,style,size,colorHex,opts={}){\n  const t=figma.createText();\n  t.name=name;\n  t.fontName={family:fam,style:style};\n  t.characters=chars;\n  t.fontSize=size;\n  if(opts.ls!==undefined)t.letterSpacing={unit:'PERCENT',value:opts.ls};\n  if(opts.lh)t.lineHeight={unit:'PIXELS',value:opts.lh};\n  t.fills=[solid(colorHex,opts.op===undefined?1:opts.op)];\n  if(opts.w){t.textAutoResize='NONE';t.resize(opts.w,opts.h||size*1.4);if(opts.align)t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align;}\n  return t;\n}\n```\nWait: fontName must be set before characters, and font must be loaded ✓.\n\nComponents:\n\n1) Button/Secondary:\n```js\nconst btnSec=figma.createComponent();\nbtnSec.name='Button /