coordinates relative after append). Resize before/after fine.\n\nComponents to build in script 1: SecondaryBtn, Header, SectionHeader, TextField, TransactionRow, FAB. \n\nPositions: lay components at y=1150: xs: 0, 400, 800, 1200, 1600, 2000. Set after creation: comp.x=..., comp.y=1150.\n\nReturn JSON ids.\n\nThen Script 2 fetches these ids.\n\nAlso — for TextField: after creating comp with layoutMode VERTICAL & width fixed: set comp.resize(343,71) AFTER layoutMode; primaryAxisSizingMode 'AUTO' (hug height), counterAxisSizingMode 'FIXED'. Input layoutAlign 'STRETCH'.\n\nOrder caution: when layoutMode set, existing children get laid; add label then input. resize before layoutMode? Do: create comp, comp.resize(343,71) first (no AL), then layoutMode='VERTICAL' — with hug it may shrink height? primaryAxisSizingMode default 'AUTO' → height hugs to 17+6+48=71 ✓ good. Width: counterAxisSizingMode 'FIXED' keeps 343 ✓.\n\nTransactionRow absolute: plain positions ✓.\n\nHeader: plain absolute ✓. Icons inside button frames: hidden default: `i.visible=false`.\n\nWait: for Wallet header, both back (left) and add (right) visible: leftBtn has back+add? I planned leftBtn contains Icon_Back and Icon_Add_Card both hidden. RightBtn contains Icon_Close, Icon_Share hidden. Wallet: left back visible; right add visible?? But I put add on left... Reassign: leftBtn: Icon_Back. rightBtn: Icon_Close + Icon_Share + Icon_Add_Card. Wallet right=add ✓; Receipt right=share ✓; sheet right=close ✓. Left only back. \n\nTitle override per instance: findOne by name 'Title'.\n\nFAB: comp 52×52 r26 fill brand, effect shadow rgba(0,99,209,0.35) radius 18 offset(0,8); icon plus white 24 at (14,14).\n\nOK writing now. Also caption helper for later scripts.\n\nAlso I should double-check gradientTransform conventions: linear gradient default direction horizontal L→R with identity [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]] ✓.\n\nVertical: [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]] ✓ (rotates 90°: maps y→x). I've used this before; trust.\n\nDiagonal for balance: keep horizontal L→R (#007AFF→#0063E0) fine.\n\nPaymentCard overlay vertical stops: 0:'#14101A' a0.55, 0.42: a0.05, 1: a0.5.\n\nNow Script 2 business comps:\n\nBalanceCard: as above. Name nodes: 'Balance Label','Balance Value','Card Meta','Chevron Circle','Chevron'.\nFont: Balance Value 28 Bold.\nShadow color {r:0,g:0.39,b:0.87,a:0.28}.\n\nPaymentCard: children named 'Balance Label'(BALANCE),'Balance Value','$25,520.00' → hmm on add-card preview hide both; name 'Card Number','Name','Expiry Label','Expiry','Network Visa'.\nWait PaymentCard top: BALANCE label y=22, value y=40; number y=104; name y=157; expiry label y=145 x=196; expiry y=157 x=196; visa (263,157).\nFor wallet card show all ✓.\n\nAddPreview comp 335×170: 'Card Number' mono 17 centered? y=62 center x: w=335 align CENTER x=0,y=62 h=22. 'Name' 'NAME ON CARD' 11 SemiBold ls8 white op .65 at (20,120); 'Expiry' 'MM / YY' 11 SemiBold ls8 white .65 at (120? middle) x=150? layout: name x=20, expiry x=150? widths: name ~90, expiry ~50. Place name (20,122), expiry (150,122)? MC logo (276,116) 39×26 → overlaps expiry at 150..200? logo 276..315 ✓ gap. bottom row: labels above values? Keep single row placeholders + small labels: 'CARD HOLDER' 8? Simplify: single row: 'NAME ON CARD' (20,124), 'MM / YY' (140,124), MC logo (276,116). Number centered y=58. Also small 'EXPENIO' wordmark top-right? skip.\nWait number 17 mono '5412 7534 0089 2216' ~ 19 chars × ~10.2px ≈ 194 wide ✓ fits 335-40.\nMono load fallback: if !mono use Inter Medium.\n\nMiniCardRow: as above.\nPromoCard: as above. title width 196 at (20,46) 2 lines.\nChartCard: as computed.\nReceiptCard: as planned.\n\nScript 3-5 build frames using instances (fetch comps by id).\n\nAmount of code per frame ~3-5k chars ✓.\n\nPrototype script: hotspots + reactions.\n\nThen screenshots.\n\nTotal ~7 use_figma calls + a few screenshots. Good. Let me go.\n\nAlso captions above frames: name 16 SemiBold ink3 at (x, 60).\n\nAlso frames: 01 at (0,100), 02 (475,100), 03 (950,100), 04 (1425,100), 05 (1900,100), 06 (2375,100).\n\nComponents row y=1150.. maybe 1200: comps heights vary; place at y=1200.\n\nAlso note: appending instance children into frames — I must append instance to frame BEFORE setting x/y? If set x,y then append, coordinates preserved as absolute→become relative? Plugin: x,y are relative to parent; setting before append then appending keeps node's x,y values (relative interpretation changes) — set AFTER append. I'll append first always.\n\nLet me write Script 1 now.\n\nOne more: recolor function touching strokes: Icon vector strokes likely [black]. ✓.\n\nAlso verify: creating instance of given Button (1:23) — get comp via getNodeByIdAsync then createInstance ✓.\n\nStatus bar/home indicator components: '1:33','1:44'.\n\nWrite Script 1.","signature":"b4a4256c9a3b402d8c38fc73"}],"id":"026e933b-4632-4449-b071-07ea8df7cc4f","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259a9f97-bab6-42ed-a1f7-e48e66488de3","uuid":"ec29a2d7-4cc7-4b51-8e92-4feb1d22105c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:37:21.172Z","thinking_duration_ms":464647}
