{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product-design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv/ (fileKey KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv). Read 「00 · Start Here」 for the task brief, follow 「01 · Foundations」 visual specs, reuse components from 「02 · Components」, use assets from 「04 · Media」, and deliver the complete design into 「03 · Workspace」. Constraints: call whoami before writing and confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (done — confirmed); preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; if an app name disagrees with the brief, use the brief's product; build exactly the 6 named frames as a clickable prototype; use the configured account only; use whoami/get_metadata/read-only use_figma to inspect, then use_figma to build, then get_screenshot to verify; inspect screenshots of all required screens and iterate; finish with the assigned file URL, the 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations. Before every tool call include a visible decision summary prefixed exactly 'Reasoning summary:'; after each tool result do the same; final response starts with 'Reasoning summary: ...' then 'Final answer:'. This is an unattended session — resolve routine choices using the brief without waiting. For the benchmark, \"read-only source\" instructions apply to preserving reference pages, not the workspace.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JavaScript, figma global, max 50000 chars per call)\n   - MCP tools: whoami, get_metadata (XML structure dumps), get_screenshot (enableBase64Response:true required since no shell access to download URLs), use_figma\n   - Component instancing across pages: figma.getNodeById(id).createInstance() — media/given components can be instanced into workspace; text overrides possible on instance children\n   - Font loading requirement: await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Inter\", style:\"Semi Bold\"}) — style is \"Semi Bold\" NOT \"SemiBold\"; load before any text creation\n   - MUST use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` to change pages; MUST NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync\n   - IMAGE fills on components (scaleMode FILL/FIT, imageHash); resize instances for cropping; cornerRadius+clipsContent for circular avatars\n   - Vector creation via figma.createVector() + vectorPaths (M/L/Q/C/Z path data) for chart curve\n   - GradientPaint with gradientTransform + gradientStops\n   - Prototype wiring via figma.getNodeById / frame.nativeElement? No — use node.prototypeStartPoint? Actual API: create interactions by setting node's prototype connections (node.prototypeConnections or via flow) — plan: use `figma.createAction`-style objects on `node.prototypeConnections` (or `node.setPrototypeConnections`... to verify in-flight) for onClick navigation between frames\n   - Light mode iOS design: 375×812, status bar 44px, home indicator 34px\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv** — 5 pages: 0:1 (00·Start Here), 1:2 (01·Foundations), 1:3 (02·Components), 1:4 (04·Media), 8:2 (03·Workspace, EMPTY — delivery target)\n   - **00·Start Here brief (page 0:1, frame 7:2)** — the spec:\n     - Product: Expenio — personal expense manager. Canvas 375×812, iPhone, light mode.\n     - \"How to work\": Build exactly 6 frames named exactly as listed (one state per frame), wire as clickable prototype. Everything in \"Must include\" must appear. Brand color + typeface fixed; all other colors/type scale/spacing/radii/elevation are mine. Build other states, headers, navigation, business components as reusable components. Use media from 04. Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" exactly.\n     - **01_Get_Started**: Goal: Understand what Expenio is and start. Must include: Actions: \"Get Started\" • App: Logo_Expenio • Copy: \"Going cashless has never been easier with the world's leading expense manager.\" • Media: Illustration_Get_Started. LINK: Get Started → 02_Home\n     - **02_Home**: Goal: See my balance, spending trend and latest transactions. Must include: Actions: open balance (Icon_Chevron_Right) · \"See all\" · new payment (Icon_Plus) • Balance: \"My Balance\" · $25,520.00 • Expenses: \"Expenses\" chart, MAR – AUG, JUN highlighted at $80.40 • Greeting: \"Hello, Maria\" · \"Home\" · Avatar_Maria_Lopez • Transactions: \"Wallet\" · 3 rows (see DATA). LINKS: open balance / See all → 03_Wallet; new payment → 05_Payment\n     - **03_Wallet**: Goal: Review my card, an offer and my transactions. Must include: Actions: \"Back\" (Icon_Back) · add card (Icon_Add_Card) • Card: Maria's Visa card · card 1 of 3 in the wallet • Header: \"Wallet\" • Promo: \"POPULAR\" · \"Get up to 15% cashback on clothing and apparel\" (Promo_Cashback) • Transactions: \"Transactions\" · 3 rows. LINKS: Back → 02_Home; add card → 04_Add_Card\n     - **04_Add_Card**: Goal: Add a new payment card. Must include: Actions: close (Icon_Close) · \"Add new card\" • Card preview: shows the number typed so far (Logo_Mastercard); name and expiry not yet entered • Form: \"Card holder's name\" (empty, placeholder \"Name on card\") · \"Card number\" 5412 7534 0089 2216, focused, Mastercard detected (Logo_Mastercard) · \"Expiry Date\" (empty, placeholder \"MM / YY\") · \"CVV\" (empty, placeholder \"123\", help Icon_Help) • Header: \"Add new card\" • Presentation: sheet over 03_Wallet. LINKS: Add new card / close → 03_Wallet\n     - **05_Payment**: Goal: Pay Robert $50.00 with my card. Must include: Actions: \"Cancel\" · \"Pay now\" • Amount: $50.00 • Card: Maria's Visa card (as on 03_Wallet) · card 1 of 3 • Header: \"Payment\" • Note: \"Add a note\" (empty) • Payee: \"PAYING\" · \"Robert Dawson\" (Avatar_Robert_Dawson). LINKS: Pay now → 06_Receipt; Cancel → 02_Home\n     - **06_Receipt**: Goal: Confirm what I paid. Must include: Actions: share (Icon_Share) · \"Home\" • Header: \"Receipt\" • Receipt: \"CASH RECEIPT\" · 20.08.2020 · Amount · Service Fee · Internet Charge · Total · barcode (Barcode_Receipt). LINK: Home → 02_Home\n     - **Navigation structure**: 01_Get_Started → Get Started → 02_Home. From 02: open balance or See all → 03_Wallet; new payment → 05_Payment → Pay now → 06_Receipt → Home → 02_Home. 04_Add_Card is a sheet over 03_Wallet. No tab bar. Entry only (no frame/link needed): transaction rows, chart points, promo, other cards in wallet, share, typing a note.\n     - **Fixed data & copy (verbatim)**: User: Maria Lopez · Avatar_Maria_Lopez. Balance: My Balance $25,520.00 (same balance printed on Maria's card). Expenses chart: Months MAR · APR · MAY · JUN · JUL · AUG; Highlighted point: JUN · $80.40. Transactions (newest first): Nike Air Max 2090 · 15 Aug 2020 · −$243.00 (Merchant_Nike); iPad Pro 2020 · 10 Aug 2020 · −$799.00 (Merchant_Apple); Uber · 5 Mar 2020 · +$50.00 (Merchant_Uber). Maria's card: Visa (Logo_Visa) · BALANCE $25,520.00 · 4225 9765 0008 6141 · MARIA LOPEZ · EXPIRY 09/24 · Artwork: Card_Texture_Coral. New card (04): Mastercard (Logo_Mastercard) · 5412 7534 0089 2216 · Holder name, expiry and CVV not yet entered. Promo: POPULAR · Get up to 15% cashback on clothing and apparel · Promo_Cashback. Payment: Paying Robert Dawson (Avatar_Robert_Dawson) · $50.00 · from Maria's Visa card. Receipt: CASH RECEIPT · 20.08.2020 · Amount $40.00 · Service Fee $2.82 · Internet Charge $7.18 · Total $50.00\n     - **Evaluation**: 1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data & copy accuracy 3. Flow & prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality & consistency of own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (focused card-number field, current card, highlighted chart point, sheet presentation)\n   - **01·Foundations (1:2)**: Brand primary #007AFF fixed; Inter for all UI text (card numbers may use monospaced face of choice); canvas 375×812 iPhone X/11 Pro; light mode only; 02_Home and 03_Wallet may scroll vertically.\n   - **02·Components (1:3)** — given components (reference IDs, use as instances):\n     - Button (1:23): 343×56, fill #007AFF (rgb 0, 0.4784, 1), cornerRadius 14, no stroke/shadow; text child 1:24 \"Get Started\" Inter Semi Bold 16, white\n     - Text Field (1:26): 343×73; label 1:27 Inter Semi Bold 14, #1A1A1F (0.102,0.102,0.122); Input frame 1:28 343×48 fill #F2F2F7 (0.949,0.949,0.969) radius 10; placeholder 1:29 Inter Regular 16, #8E8E93 (0.557,0.557,0.576)\n     - Status Bar (1:33): 375×44; \"9:41\" Inter Semi Bold 15 black; Notch rect 209×30 black; Signal/Wifi/Battery glyphs black\n     - Home Indicator (1:44): 375×34; black rect 134×5, radius 3\n   - **04·Media (1:4, frame 6:12)** — all COMPONENT nodes (instance them):\n     - Logo_Expenio (6:10): 181×24 vector wordmark (black)\n     - Card_Texture_Coral (5:10): 276×160, IMAGE fill FILL (hash 8f113a3b4e92a47baa59c020e548650be6620214)\n     - Illustration_Get_Started (5:6): 240×160, IMAGE FILL (hash 1e73e6a220530feb25c145755ffbc31fbe1be98b)\n     - Promo_Cashback (5:8): 213×160, IMAGE FILL (hash 3c019e19ae95c6809caf8520f14bc19f14bb67d6)\n     - Avatar_Maria_Lopez (5:4): 108×72 (NOT square — resize to square for circle), IMAGE FILL (hash 10428034d4e14f68c79d05bd1e6835393580751c)\n     - Avatar_Robert_Dawson (5:2): 72×72, IMAGE FILL (hash 0e33a4c323f4c975a2d05e83a79b82151f6f5405)\n     - Merchant_Apple (5:5) 96×72, Merchant_Nike (5:9) 72×72, Merchant_Uber (5:7) 118×72 — IMAGE FIT, black logos\n     - Logo_Mastercard (6:11): 39×26, vector circles with brand colors\n     - Logo_Visa (5:3): 222×72, IMAGE FIT, white logo\n     - Barcode_Receipt (6:2): 254×68, black vector bars\n     - Icons (24×24 vector line icons, #1A1A1F, recolorable): Icon_Add_Card 6:6, Icon_Back 6:3, Icon_Chevron_Right 6:4, Icon_Close 6:7, Icon_Help 6:5, Icon_Plus 6:8, Icon_Share 6:9\n     - Media page note: \"Icons are neutral (#1A1A1F) line icons — recolor them to fit your color system; the Mastercard and Visa marks keep their brand colors (Logo_Visa is white, shown on gray).\"\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Invalid sessionId on get_metadata**: Passed sessionId \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\" → error \"Invalid sessionId. Retry this tool call without sessionId, or call create_session and use its returned UUID as sessionId.\" Fixed by omitting sessionId on all subsequent calls (create_session is not among available tools; all calls work without sessionId).\n   - **Screenshot URL unusable**: First get_screenshot of 6:12 returned only a URL + curl instructions, but no shell tool is available to download it. Fixed by re-calling with enableBase64Response:true to get the image inline. All future screenshots must use enableBase64Response:true.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed account identity and file access (zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai, Full seat on \"Sensenova design\" enterprise org).\n   - Fully extracted brief, specs, component styles, and media asset structure via metadata + read-only use_figma inspection + inline screenshot.\n   - Verified 03·Workspace (page 8:2) is empty — will build everything there.\n   - Design system decisions made (mine to define): background #F2F2F7/#F7F7FA, surface #FFFFFF, text primary #1A1A1F, secondary #6E6E78, placeholder #8E8E93, input fill #F2F2F7, divider #E8E8EE, positive green #34C759, error #FF3B30; radii 10 (inputs), 12–16 (cards), 14 (buttons, matching given), 24 (sheet top); soft shadow 0 8 24 rgba(26,26,31,0.06); type scale: balance 32 Bold, titles 24 Bold, section 20 SemiBold, headline 16 SemiBold, body 16 Regular, 14 sub, 12 caption; card number monospace (try Roboto Mono, try/catch fallback to Inter).\n   - Component architecture plan (build in workspace): ButtonPrimary/ButtonSecondary (343×56 r14), IconButton (44×44 white circle + icon instance), SectionHeader (title + \"See all\"), TransactionRow (44 icon tile + title/date + amount), BalanceCard (blue hero card, \"My Balance\" $25,520.00, chevron), ExpensesChart card (vector curve MAR–AUG, JUN highlighted $80.40), PromoCard, PaymentCard (Visa coral card + pagination dots 1 of 3), mini card row for 05, TextField base with label+input; instance given Status Bar (1:33), Home Indicator (1:44), and all media components.\n   - Build order plan: (1) switch to page 8:2, load fonts, build components; (2) 01_Get_Started; (3) 02_Home; (4) 03_Wallet; (5) 04_Add_Card (wallet top dimmed + sheet, focused card-number field with brand border, MC logo in field); (6) 05_Payment; (7) 06_Receipt; (8) prototype wiring; (9) screenshots of all 6 frames + fixes.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (paraphrased with all constraints intact): 请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv/ 。请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。Plus the benchmark system instructions: use only the assigned file; whoami before writing, confirm zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; read 00·Start Here (brief wins on app name); read 01·Foundations (fonts/colors fixed); reuse 02·Components and 04·Media; preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; create the complete design inside 03·Workspace (create if missing; frames/components/prototype connections allowed even if empty); read-only-source instructions apply to reference pages, not workspace; keep unrelated content intact; no different file or account; workflow whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma → use_figma build → get_screenshot verify; no delegating to other agents; fonts/gradients/shadows/blurs allowed per requirements; load fonts before text; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions after screens exist; inspect screenshots of all screens and fix; finish with file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work, limitations; unattended session — don't wait; before every tool call write a 'Reasoning summary:' line; final response format 'Reasoning summary: ...' then 'Final answer:'.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Build the full design in page 8:2 (03·Workspace): design tokens/styles, reusable components, the 6 frames (01_Get_Started, 02_Home, 03_Wallet, 04_Add_Card, 05_Payment, 06_Receipt) at 375×812 light mode\n   - Wire prototype connections: 01→02 (Get Started); 02 balance/chevron + See all →03, FAB/plus →05; 03 Back →02, add-card →04; 04 Add new card + close →03; 05 Pay now →06, Cancel →02; 06 Home →02\n   - Screenshot-verify all 6 screens, fix visible problems, re-verify\n   - Final response with file URL, workspace page ID (8:2), screen IDs, prototype work summary, limitations\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Completed all read-only inspection. The last action was a read-only use_figma dump of media component internals (IDs 5:2, 5:4, 5:10, 5:6, 5:8, 5:3, 6:11, 6:2, 5:5, 5:9, 5:7, 6:10, and icons 6:6, 6:3, 6:4, 6:7, 6:5, 6:8, 6:9), confirming: all are COMPONENT nodes; photo assets (avatars, Card_Texture_Coral, Illustration_Get_Started, Promo_Cashback, merchants, Logo_Visa) are single-frame components with IMAGE fills (FILL or FIT mode) and no children; Logo_Expenio, Logo_Mastercard, Barcode_Receipt, and the 7 icons are vector-based components; Avatar_Maria_Lopez is 108×72 so it needs resizing to a square (e.g. 44×44) for circular avatar use; icons are 24×24 with vector children (mostly stroke-style, recolorable). Nothing has been written to the file yet. Reasoning summaries have been included before every tool call as required.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin the build phase in 03·Workspace (page 8:2), per my stated plan: \"Implementation approach with use_figma: Multiple calls... 1. Setup: load fonts... a. Create text styles + color styles... b. Build base components... 2. Build 01_Get_Started... 8. Prototype wiring. 9. Screenshots + fixes.\" First use_figma call: switch to page 8:2 via `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync()`, load Inter fonts (Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold) and monospace (Roboto Mono Medium with try/catch), create paint/text styles, and build the core reusable components (ButtonPrimary, ButtonSecondary, IconButton, SectionHeader, TransactionRow, BalanceCard, ChartCard, PromoCard, PaymentCard, TextField) using instances of the given components (1:33, 1:44, 1:23, 1:26) and media components (6:10, 5:10, 5:6, 5:8, 5:4, 5:2, 5:5, 5:9, 5:7, 6:11, 5:3, 6:2, 6:3–6:9), then proceed screen by screen.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/10case-6models-v4-20261101/runs/TEST-035_1793485526172/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-10case-6models-v4-20261101-workspace/259a9f97-bab6-42ed-a1f7-e48e66488de3.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259a9f97-bab6-42ed-a1f7-e48e66488de3","uuid":"09982bf2-27d3-44ec-a4b9-d06320b7a25e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:39:52.535Z","isSynthetic":true}
