{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product-design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv/ (fileKey KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv). Requirements (verbatim constraints preserved):\n   - Call whoami before writing and confirm assigned account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE — confirmed earlier: Full seat, \"Sensenova design\" org).\n   - Read 「00 · Start Here」 for product, exact screens, states, data, copy, prototype requirements. Read 「01 · Foundations」 for visual rules (brand #007AFF, Inter; card numbers may be monospace; 375×812 light mode). Reuse 「02 · Components」 components; use 「04 · Media」 assets. Preserve ALL reference pages and their existing nodes.\n   - Deliver the complete design inside 「03 · Workspace」 (page 8:2). \"Read-only source\" instructions apply to reference pages, NOT the workspace. Keep unrelated content intact; no different file/account.\n   - Build exactly 6 frames as clickable prototype: 01_Get_Started, 02_Home, 03_Wallet, 04_Add_Card (sheet over 03), 05_Payment, 06_Receipt. Fixed copy/data verbatim: \"Get Started\"; \"Going cashless has never been easier with the world's leading expense manager.\"; \"My Balance\" $25,520.00; \"Hello, Maria\"; \"Home\"; \"Expenses\" chart MAR–AUG with JUN highlighted $80.40; \"Wallet\"; transactions newest-first: Nike Air Max 2090 · 15 Aug 2020 · −$243.00; iPad Pro 2020 · 10 Aug 2020 · −$799.00; Uber · 5 Mar 2020 · +$50.00; \"See all\"; Maria's Visa card BALANCE $25,520.00 · 4225 9765 0008 6141 · MARIA LOPEZ · EXPIRY 09/24 · card 1 of 3; \"POPULAR\" · \"Get up to 15% cashback on clothing and apparel\"; \"Back\"; add card; \"Transactions\"; \"Add new card\" header + action; card preview shows number typed so far (5412 7534 0089 2216, Mastercard detected), name/expiry not entered; form fields \"Card holder's name\" (placeholder \"Name on card\"), \"Card number\" (focused), \"Expiry Date\" (placeholder \"MM / YY\"), \"CVV\" (placeholder \"123\", Icon_Help); sheet over 03_Wallet; \"Payment\"; \"PAYING\" Robert Dawson $50.00 from Maria's Visa (card 1 of 3); \"Add a note\" (empty); \"Cancel\"/\"Pay now\"; \"Receipt\"; \"CASH RECEIPT\" · 20.08.2020 · Amount $40.00 · Service Fee $2.82 · Internet Charge $7.18 · Total $50.00 · barcode; share; \"Home\".\n   - Prototype links: 01→02 (Get Started); 02: open balance/chevron + See all →03, new payment →05; 03: Back →02, add card →04; 04: Add new card + close →03; 05: Pay now →06, Cancel →02; 06: Home →02. Entry-only (no links): transaction rows, chart points, promo, other cards, share, note typing. No tab bar.\n   - Workflow: whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma → use_figma build → get_screenshot verify all screens; iterate on visible problems; fonts loaded before text; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions after screens exist.\n   - Unattended session: resolve routine choices per brief without waiting; report real limitations if blocked.\n   - Output format rule: before EVERY tool call include a visible decision summary prefixed exactly 'Reasoning summary:'; after each tool result the same; final response starts 'Reasoning summary: ...' then 'Final answer:' with file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - mcp__figma__use_figma: JS via Figma Plugin API (figma global), max 50000 chars per call, AND max ~48000-byte RETURN value (exceeding it discards/rolls back that run's edits — keep returns tiny, e.g. return 'OK').\n   - CRITICAL discovered behavior: nodes set visible=false in a main component are ABSENT/unfindable in instances (findOne returns null; instance children array omits them). Rule: any node needing per-instance override (text, visibility, fills, strokes) must be VISIBLE in the component; use sibling overlays instead of hidden-slot toggles.\n   - `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)` (async form); `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` at start of every script (currentPage persistence across calls is unreliable); forbidden: loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync.\n   - Fonts: await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Regular'|'Medium'|'Semi Bold'|'Bold'}) — \"Semi Bold\" with space; Roboto Mono Medium loads OK (used for card numbers).\n   - Component instancing across pages (media/given components), text/style overrides on instance children (visible only), instance resize for image FILL crops, cornerRadius on instance roots for circular avatars.\n   - Icon recolor: for each vector in icon instance, if strokes.length set strokes, if fills.length set fills (try/catch per vector).\n   - Prototype wiring: node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'DISSOLVE',duration:0.25} | {type:'MOVE_IN'|'MOVE_OUT', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:0.3}}}].\n   - Vector curve via figma.createVector() + vectorPaths (Catmull-Rom→Bezier path, absolute coords, then v.x=0,v.y=0).\n   - GRADIENT_LINEAR with gradientTransform ([[1,0,0],[0,1,0]] horizontal; [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]] vertical).\n   - get_screenshot requires enableBase64Response:true (no shell to download URLs).\n   - Design system (mine): bg #F5F5F9, surface #FFFFFF, input #F2F2F7, ink #1A1A1F, ink2 #6C6C74, ink3 #9A9AA3, placeholder #8E8E93, divider #E9E9EF/#EDEDF2, brand #007AFF→#0063E0, coral badge #FFE9E0/#BF4A2B, success #34C759; radii 10 inputs, 12 tiles, 14 buttons, 16 cards, 20 receipt, 28 sheet top; soft shadow rgba(26,26,31,0.08) 0/8/20.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file KGjmNajqa9on8PzOkCc7Tv; delive