{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the real problem! This Figma environment uses a NEWER/different reaction schema:\n\n- Trigger type must be 'ON_CLICK' (not 'CLICK')\n- Action type for node navigation: the error says 'NODE' is invalid... wait, let me re-read.\n\nThe error lists accepted action types:\n1. 'CONDITIONAL' with conditionalBlocks\n2. 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' — hmm interesting, \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\". So one variant of action.type is BACK or CLOSE.\n3. 'URL' with url\n4. 'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME' variants\n5. One variant seems to accept destinationId/navigation/transition? Let me look: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched: Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing ... Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' ... Expected null, received object at [0].action.transition\"\n\nSo there IS a variant that has a transition — that would be the NODE navigation action. The validation for that variant: destinationId seems accepted there (no \"unrecognized key\" complaint in that branch — actually the branch complaints listed \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" for BACK/CLOSE, URL, SET_VARIABLE etc. But the transition-specific branch complains about transition.easing and transition.type DISSOLVE being invalid).\n\nSo for the NODE action variant:\n- transition.type must be one of 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT' — DISSOLVE is not in the enum! Interesting. So in this API version, transitions are limited to those 5 types? That's odd — real Figma supports DISSOLVE, SMART_ANIMATE, INSTANT, etc. But this environment's validator only accepts MOVE_IN, MOVE_OUT, PUSH, SLIDE_IN, SLIDE_OUT.\n- transition requires 'easing' (Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing)\n- Also transition requires direction/matchLayers for some types.\n\nAnd for the trigger: type must be 'ON_CLICK' (not 'CLICK').\n\nSo the fix:\n- trigger: {type: 'ON_CLICK'}\n- action: {type: 'NODE', destinationId, navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: {type: 'SLIDE_IN' etc., easing: ...}}\n\nWhat's the easing schema? In real Figma plugin API: easing: {type: 'EASE_IN_AND_OUT' | 'EASE_IN' | 'EASE_OUT' | 'LINEAR' | 'EASE_IN_BACK' | ...} or {type:'GENTLE'...}? Actually in newer API, transition easing is {type: 'EASE_OUT'} etc. Let me guess: easing: {type: 'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'}. Or maybe easing accepts {easingFunction:...}. The validator just says \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" — so I need to provide an easing object. Try {type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'} first; if invalid, error message will tell me the accepted values.\n\nAlso DISSOLVE is rejected → use 'MOVE_IN'/'MOVE_OUT' with direction, or 'PUSH' with direction. For screen-to-screen navigation, PUSH direction LEFT might be nice; for the sheet, MOVE_IN from BOTTOM and MOVE_OUT to BOTTOM.\n\nAlso note: for MOVE_OUT you need direction too probably. Let me structure:\n\n- Default link: transition {type:'PUSH', direction:'LEFT', easing:{type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'}, duration? } Hmm does it need duration? The error didn't complain about duration. Real Figma transitions have duration (seconds) except for SMART_ANIMATE default. I'll include duration: 0.3.\n\nWait, but also matchLayers was mentioned: \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.direction / matchLayers / easing\" — that was for the branch where type mismatched. The requirements per type:\n- MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT: direction required\n- PUSH: direction required\n- SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT: direction required\n- easing required for all\n- matchLayers probably only for SMART_ANIMATE (not in enum here).\n\nLet me test one link with:\n{n.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId:'15:95', navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'PUSH', direction:'LEFT', easing:{type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'}, duration:0.3}}}]}\n\nIf easing type invalid, the error will list accepted easing types.\n\nAlso note the earlier 48KB return mystery: the thrown validation error message is HUGE (~48KB). When link() threw inside my try/catch... wait, in the first failed run I DID catch errors into errs[]. But the error here was thrown at \"set (<input>:78:11)\" — this test had no try/catch so it propagated as tool error. In the earlier runs, the try/catch caught it and errs joined into my return string — THAT's why the return was 48KB! errs contained 11 copies of this giant validation message. Mystery solved.\n\nSo with correct schema, no errors, tiny returns.\n\nNow the destination 'I15:137;15:72' (See all text inside instance) — setting reactions on instance children may throw a different error (\"Cannot set reactions on node inside instance\"?). Actually in real Figma API, you CAN'T set reactions on instance children (they're read-only). If it fails, I'll overlay a transparent rectangle on top of 'See all' in the screen and link that instead.\n\nLet me test the corrected schema on one link first.","signature":"a91b411a682741969aa1cb9a"}],"id":"bb536cc7-fe42-444e-a826-a280938ebe50","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259a9f97-bab6-42ed-a1f7-e48e66488de3","uuid":"51bb5107-1396-4030-8ddc-108fee3b716c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:51:40.675Z","thinking_duration_ms":23214}
